---
import Layout from "@components/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "@components/PageHeader.astro";
import { Card, Grid, Timeline, TimelineItem } from "webcoreui/astro";
import DecklistTooltip from "@components/DecklistTooltip.astro";
import DeckSection from "@components/DeckSection.astro";
import { tomVanDeLogtDeck, achiIIesDeck } from "@data/decklists";
---

<Layout
    title="History - Replenish Guide"
    description="Explore the rich history of the Replenish deck in Magic: The Gathering. From its Type 2 origins in 2000 to the dramatic errata changes and its resilience after the Parallax Tide ban."
>
    <PageHeader
        title="History of the Deck"
        description="The story of Replenish spans over two decades. From its dominance in Type 2 (Standard) at the turn of the millennium, to its rebirth in Premodern fueled by rules changes, and finally its resilience in the face of bans. Here is a look at the archetypes' defining milestones."
        imageSrc="/src/assets/banners/parallax_wave.jpeg"
        imageAlt="Parallax Wave"
        imageCaption="Parallax Wave by Greg Staples"
        isCard={true}
    />
    <div style="margin-top: 3rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <Timeline>
            <TimelineItem title="1. The Standard Origins (2000)" titleTag="h2">
                <p>
                    Replenish first made waves at the highest levels of
                    competitive Magic during the 2000 World Championship. Hall
                    of Famer Tom van de Logt piloted this list to a Top 8
                    finish. This Type 2 list leaned on fast mana like <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Sky Diamond">Sky Diamond</a
                    > and <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Rishadan Port">Rishadan Port</a
                    > to slow opponents down, while using <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Mystical Tutor">Mystical Tutor</a
                    > and <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Enlightened Tutor">Enlightened Tutor</a
                    > for immense consistency. A single <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Energy Field">Energy Field</a
                    > could buy infinite time until the combo was ready.
                </p>

                <Card>
                    <div
                        style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"
                    >
                        <div>
                            <h3
                                style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--w-color-primary-10);"
                            >
                                2000 World Championship (Standard)
                            </h3>
                            <p
                                style="margin: 0.25rem 0 0 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-40);"
                            >
                                Played by Tom van de Logt
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <Grid column={{ md: 3 }} gap="lg">
                        {tomVanDeLogtDeck.columns.map((col) => (
                            <div>
                                {col.sections.map((sec) => (
                                    <DeckSection
                                        title={sec.title}
                                        items={sec.items}
                                    />
                                ))}
                            </div>
                        ))}
                    </Grid>
                </Card>
            </TimelineItem>

            <TimelineItem
                title="2. The Parallax Tide Era (Pre-Ban Jan 2026)"
                titleTag="h2"
            >
                <p>
                    As the Premodern format developed, players realized that <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Parallax Tide">Parallax Tide</a
                    > could be weaponized to permanently exile an opponent's lands
                    just as easily as Wave exiled creatures. By late 2025 and early
                    2026, Parallax Tide Replenish dominated competitive play. To secure
                    complete control in mirrors and against interaction, pilots like
                    AchiIIes adapted by running cards like <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Tsabo's Web">Tsabo's Web</a
                    > and four copies of <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a
                    > in the main deck—creating a stifling one-sided lock right before
                    the hammer fell.
                </p>
                <Card>
                    <div
                        style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"
                    >
                        <div>
                            <h3
                                style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--w-color-primary-10);"
                            >
                                MTGO Premodern League #10124 (Jan 2026)
                            </h3>
                            <p
                                style="margin: 0.25rem 0 0 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-40);"
                            >
                                Played by AchiIIes (Day Before Ban)
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <Grid column={{ md: 3 }} gap="lg">
                        {achiIIesDeck.columns.map((col) => (
                            <div>
                                {col.sections.map((sec) => (
                                    <DeckSection
                                        title={sec.title}
                                        items={sec.items}
                                    />
                                ))}
                            </div>
                        ))}
                    </Grid>
                </Card>
            </TimelineItem>

            <TimelineItem
                title="3. The Post-Ban Resurgence (2026 - Present)"
                titleTag="h2"
            >
                <p>
                    On January 18, 2026, format curator Martin Berlin banned
                    Parallax Tide, citing its oppressive, repetitive play
                    patterns and insurmountable win rates. The community wrote
                    the deck off, assuming it was dead without its primary lock
                    piece.
                </p>
                <p>
                    However, dedicated pilots proved them wrong. By replacing
                    Tide with <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Decree of Silence">Decree of Silence</a
                    > and incorporating flexible protection like <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Abeyance">Abeyance</a
                    > and <a
                        href="#"
                        class="card-hover"
                        data-card-name="Mana Leak">Mana Leak</a
                    >, the deck evolved from a pure combo lock into a resilient
                    combo-control hybrid.
                </p>
                <p>
                    This new iteration reached its definitive proving ground on
                    May 1, 2026, when
                    <strong>Brian Siu</strong> piloted Parallax Replenish to victory
                    at the
                    <strong
                        >North American Premodern Championship at Lobstercon
                        2026</strong
                    >, silencing doubters and cementing the archetype's status
                    as a top-tier powerhouse.
                </p>
                <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                    To explore Brian Siu's championship decklist and other
                    refined post-ban configurations, check out our interactive <a
                        href="/deck"
                        style="color: var(--w-color-info); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: bold;"
                        >Lists page</a
                    >.
                </p>
            </TimelineItem>
        </Timeline>
    </div>
    <DecklistTooltip />
</Layout>
